{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the flesh of the thanksgiving-offering's shelamim.</b> The text speaks here of all shelamim. One may say that since the thanksgiving-offering is also <b>שלמים</b>, as it is written: <b>זבח תודה שלמיו</b>, therefore it is called <b>שלמים</b>. And if you say: does this not refer to the other shelamim (i.e., the vow and the freewill offering)? The verse states <b>תודת</b> — and it is written (below, v. 16): <b>ואם נדר או נדבה זבח קרבנו</b> without <b>שלמיו</b>, to include the thanksgiving-offering among the shelamim that are eaten for two days and one night. But according to the plain sense, the thanksgiving-offering is the subject, as it says: <b>ובשר זבח תודת שלמיו</b>. And the Rabbis expounded from here that a <b>תודה</b> is eaten for one day and one night."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The bracketed lemma indicates a very short source comment; the full Hebrew text supplied here follows the standard Chizkuni on this verse. The Hebrew appears somewhat abbreviated and possibly corrupt in places; translated hyper-literally where the syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:32.515214334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}